.TH WIREGLOW 1 "October 2026" "Wireglow" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wireglow \- desktop client for Free Turn Proxy connections
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wireglow
.SH DESCRIPTION
Wireglow manages connection profiles and local or GNOME system proxy sessions
using its bundled controller, free-turn-proxy and mihomo engines.
A graphical session and a running systemd user manager are required.
.SH UPGRADING
Close Wireglow and wait for proxy recovery to finish before upgrading or
removing the package. The installer does not stop running clients.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wireglow/
Profiles, preferences and the proxy recovery journal. XDG_CONFIG_HOME overrides
the configuration base directory. Package removal preserves these files.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wireglow/
Temporary session files. The fallback is /run/user/<uid>/wireglow/.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/wireglow/README.Debian
